      "id": "interpol-pda-g1",
      "type": "background",
      "headline": "A debut single that didn't chart",
      "snippet": "\"PDA\" was the debut single from the American rock band Interpol. It came out on August 22, 2002, as the lead single from their first studio album, Turn on the Bright Lights. Christopher Mills directed its music video. The two singles that followed, \"Obstacle 1\" and \"Say Hello to the Angels\" / \"NYC\", both charted. \"PDA\" did not.",
      "context": "First single from the debut album.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Wikipedia",
        "platform": "wikipedia"
      },
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PDA_(Interpol_song)",
      "sourceDate": "2026-08-16"
    },
    {
      "id": "interpol-pda-g2",
      "type": "background",
      "headline": "One of the band's oldest songs",
      "snippet": "\"PDA\" is one of the oldest songs in Interpol's catalog, and it existed well before Turn on the Bright Lights. The band recorded it on their first demo tape. It then turned up on several early EPs: Fukd ID #3, Precipitate and the self-titled Interpol EP. The 2002 single was therefore not the first time the song had been released.",
      "context": "Explains why fans hear demo versions with different lyrics.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Wikipedia",
        "platform": "wikipedia"
      },
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PDA_(Interpol_song)",
      "sourceDate": "2026-08-16"
    },
